  to Moli&egrave;re) to head the cast of his razor-sharp new adaptation of
  <em>The Imaginary Invalid</em>, a comedy that proves hypochondria never
  goes out of style. <br /><br />Professional patient Argan indulges his
  every ailment, and schemes to marry off his daughter to a doctor to save
  on medical bills. But she has another life in mind. With a fearless
  ensemble directed by Broadway veteran Brandon J. Dirden, this fiercely
  funny production is about to prove that real life is what happens while
  you and your family are making other plans.</p>
END:VEVENT
